{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — who is near to me. For David composed this psalm when he fell ill and recovered from his illness, or it was by way of prophecy concerning Israel, who are in exile, like the sick. And if according to the first way, David also prophesied that he would be healed, like the prayer of Jonah. Moreover, I will add to look, and on account of sin HaShem reproves with illnesses, as it says: 'In reproofs for sin You chastise a man.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The phrase אף אוסיף להביט is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The verse citation at the end is Psalms 39:12."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:08.291861840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}